From: Jean-Michael Celerier <jmcelerier@sat.qc.ca>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 22:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rhi: gl: do not clear stencil when the attachment has none

QRhiGles2::beginPass() unconditionally adds GL_STENCIL_BUFFER_BIT to the
glClear mask whenever the render target has a depth-stencil attachment:

    if (rtD->dsAttCount && wantsDsClear)
        clearCmd.args.clear.mask |= GL_DEPTH_BUFFER_BIT | GL_STENCIL_BUFFER_BIT;

But a QRhiTextureRenderTarget's depth attachment does not have to carry
stencil. QRhiTextureRenderTargetDescription::setDepthTexture() accepts
QRhiTexture::D16, D24 and D32F, and QGles2TextureRenderTarget::create()
already knows the difference: it only calls glFramebufferTexture2D() /
glFramebufferTextureLayer() for GL_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT when
isStencilSupportingFormat() says so. So for a D32F depth texture the FBO
has a depth attachment and no stencil attachment, and every beginPass()
that clears asks the driver to clear a buffer that is not there.

That is a no-op per the GL spec, but it is a diagnosable one, and drivers
that implement KHR_debug thoroughly report it. On NVIDIA:

    GL_DEBUG_TYPE_OTHER, GL_DEBUG_SEVERITY_LOW, API source:
    "Usage warning: glClear() called with GL_STENCIL_BUFFER_BIT, but
     there is no stencil buffer. Operation will have no effect."

Measured on the ossia/score OpenGL render engine, whose intermediate
render targets use a D32F depth texture (reverse-Z: a fixed-point D24 has
strictly worse precision under a reversed depth range): 620 such messages
across the 53-test gfx suite, one per pass per frame, drowning out the
rest of the debug output.

Record whether the depth-stencil attachment actually has a stencil buffer
when the FBO is built - mirroring the conditions that decide whether
GL_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT is attached at all - and mask the clear bit on it.
The default is true, so the swapchain path (whose depth-stencil is always
a packed-format renderbuffer) and the renderbuffer attachment path are
unchanged.

No behaviour change: clearing a buffer that does not exist has no effect
by definition, so this only removes the request.
---
--- a/src/gui/rhi/qrhigles2.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/rhi/qrhigles2.cpp
@@ -5020,8 +5020,11 @@
     clearCmd.args.clear.mask = 0;
     if (rtD->colorAttCount && wantsColorClear)
         clearCmd.args.clear.mask |= GL_COLOR_BUFFER_BIT;
-    if (rtD->dsAttCount && wantsDsClear)
-        clearCmd.args.clear.mask |= GL_DEPTH_BUFFER_BIT | GL_STENCIL_BUFFER_BIT;
+    if (rtD->dsAttCount && wantsDsClear) {
+        clearCmd.args.clear.mask |= GL_DEPTH_BUFFER_BIT;
+        if (rtD->dsHasStencil)
+            clearCmd.args.clear.mask |= GL_STENCIL_BUFFER_BIT;
+    }
     clearCmd.args.clear.c[0] = colorClearValue.redF();
     clearCmd.args.clear.c[1] = colorClearValue.greenF();
     clearCmd.args.clear.c[2] = colorClearValue.blueF();
@@ -6575,6 +6578,7 @@
     if (hasDepthStencil) {
         if (m_desc.depthStencilBuffer()) {
             QGles2RenderBuffer *depthRbD = QRHI_RES(QGles2RenderBuffer, m_desc.depthStencilBuffer());
+            d.dsHasStencil = true;
             if (rhiD->caps.needsDepthStencilCombinedAttach) {
                 rhiD->f->glFramebufferRenderbuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, GL_DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT, GL_RENDERBUFFER,
                                                    depthRbD->renderbuffer);
@@ -6596,6 +6600,7 @@
             }
         } else {
             QGles2Texture *depthTexD = QRHI_RES(QGles2Texture, m_desc.depthTexture());
+            d.dsHasStencil = rhiD->isStencilSupportingFormat(depthTexD->format());
             if (multiViewCount < 2) {
                 if (depthTexD->samples > 1 && rhiD->caps.glesMultisampleRenderToTexture && m_desc.depthResolveTexture()) {
                     // Special path for GLES and
@@ -6666,6 +6671,9 @@
                                                                               multiViewCount);
                         }
                     } else {
+                        // The throwaway texture is D24S8 regardless of the
+                        // format requested for the depth attachment.
+                        d.dsHasStencil = true;
                         if (!nonMsaaThrowawayDepthTexture) {
                             rhiD->f->glGenTextures(1, &nonMsaaThrowawayDepthTexture);
                             rhiD->f->glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D_ARRAY, nonMsaaThrowawayDepthTexture);
--- a/src/gui/rhi/qrhigles2_p.h
+++ b/src/gui/rhi/qrhigles2_p.h
@@ -185,6 +185,7 @@
     int sampleCount = 1;
     int colorAttCount = 0;
     int dsAttCount = 0;
+    bool dsHasStencil = true;
     bool srgbUpdateAndBlend = false;
     QRhiRenderTargetAttachmentTracker::ResIdList currentResIdList;
     std::optional<QRhiSwapChain::StereoTargetBuffer> stereoTarget;
